---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import FinalCta from '../components/FinalCta.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Rokko — Built for the work between the office and the field"
  description="Rokko is being built to help home-service owners find answers, clear stuck work, and stay in charge of important changes."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="About Rokko"
    title="Built for the gap between knowing and getting it done."
    deck="Rokko is being built for home-service owners who are tired of chasing job details, follow-ups, and approvals across too many places."
    tone="moss"
  />

  <section class="section origin">
    <div class="container--content origin__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why we’re building it</p>
        <h2>Most shops don’t need another piece of software.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="deck">They need the tools they already have to stop hiding the answer. Job notes live in one place. Customer messages live in another. The person who can make the call is somewhere else.</p>
        <p>Rokko brings the details together, puts the next step in front of the right person, and leaves the final call with your team.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--paper principles">
    <div class="container--content">
      <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="numbered-card"><span class="numbered-card__number">01</span><h3>Show the facts</h3><p>If we make a claim or show a result, you should be able to check where it came from.</p></article>
        <article class="numbered-card"><span class="numbered-card__number">02</span><h3>Keep people in charge</h3><p>Important changes should always show who owns the call and whether it was approved.</p></article>
        <article class="numbered-card"><span class="numbered-card__number">03</span><h3>Fix real headaches</h3><p>Rokko earns its place by saving time and clearing stuck work—not by putting on an AI show.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section commitment">
    <div class="container--content commitment__grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Our promise about promises</p><h2>If we can’t back it up, we won’t print it.</h2></div>
      <p class="deck">Prices, customer stories, legal terms, and security claims stay off the site until the facts are approved. We’d rather leave a blank than sell you a guess.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FinalCta title="Show us the question your crew keeps asking." />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .origin__grid,
  .commitment__grid { display: grid; gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 8rem); align-items: start; }
  .origin h2,
  .commitment h2 { max-width: 12ch; }
  .principles .numbered-card { min-height: 21rem; }
  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .origin__grid,
    .commitment__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
  }
</style>
